function walkUp(...) {
	let prev = "";
	let stuck = 0;
	let page = 0;
	let handled = 0;   // items processed in current pass
	scrollToEdge(...bottom);
	for (let turn = 0; ...) {
		...
		// after processing
		if (pending.size === 0) break;
		if (reread) continue;   // bump moved card; screen changed
		const key = ...
		if (page > 0 && key !== "" && key === prev) {
			// 목록이 위 끝에 닿았다. 끌어올리기 창을 닫을 때 목록이 맨 위로 되돌아가므로, 아직 남은 글이 있으면 맨 아래부터 다시 걷는다.
			if (handled === 0) break;
			handled = 0;
			prev = "";
			page = 0;
			stuck = 0;
			scrollToEdge(serial, exec, ops, "bottom");
			continue;
		}
		...
	}
}
```

Wait, but swipe moves 2 items; going up from bottom to top then restarting bottom each pass is O(n/2) dumps per pass, and number of passes = number of items + 1. For 3 items that's fine. In real usage likely also acceptable but maybe expensive. But whatever the test demands — the test requires all middle items tapped, so restart is needed.

Hmm, but is there a cheaper approach matching the intended fix? Perhaps intended: after handling an item (bump or cooldown-tip), the list resets to the top, so instead of swiping back (up), we should scroll to bottom again. That is: after any handled item, the walk should return to bottom and walk up from there. That is the same as restarting. Test "진전이 없으면..." — an item not found in the list → no handled item → continue swiping up until stuck → stop. Fine.

So we can restart whenever an item was handled, regardless of key comparisons? For the reset test: page0 {글8,글9} → handled 글9 → restart bottom → new pass: {글8,글9} not pending ... then swiping up reaches 글5 → handled → restart bottom → ... 글4 → handled → restart bottom → pass with no handling → swipe up until stuck → stop. Works too, but reread already triggers `continue` for bumps (not for skip/cooldown though). The cooldown skip in this test: done="skip" and reread stays false. So it would continue processing the stale dump's 글8 (not pending) then swipe back → wrong screen state.

Hmm, but with restart-on-stuck approach we handle it. Let me think about which is more robust and simplest: implement the "repeat key → restart from bottom if progress was made this pass" logic.

Careful: after a handled item that reset the list to top, going up eventually reaches the top and repeats a key. But the keys seen right after reset may coincide with keys seen in the same pass earlier if the pass started at bottom of a short list. E.g. 4 titles: pass starts bottom {글2,글3}, handle 글3 → reset top. Next turn {글0,글1} — that's a new key (not seen this pass). Swipe back no move → repeat {글0,글1} → stuck → restart bottom. Good.

But another subtlety: in reset test, after page2 repeat detection we restart. But note prev tracking also counts for the same-pass skip. Reset prev="" and page=0 so no false repeat.

Additionally limit total passes to avoid infinite loops: handled check ensures termination as long as each pass either handles something (pending shrinks) or stops. Since handled items are deleted from pending, and a pass handles ≥1, passes ≤ pending+1. Good.

But there's a subtle bug: `reread` for bump handling triggers `continue` without swiping; then the next read at the same list position... after a bump the card moves to top, but sheet closes → list resets to top anyway. Reread continues at whatever position now. That's existing behavior; tests "처리 순서" pass currently. Adding restart shouldn't break them. Let me check "처리 순서" test that walks: fixtures list, taps... Let me check remaining tests to ensure behavior preservation.

